7592186108706 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cc1a15c3-176a-5276-8829-8127fd83a205" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186108707 #edb/ref 1080 "images/6a/6a3717a85c76d0c969184f2cd6d67bca0e394e73d73e2b0e1f9bac54ef47b0c0.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186108707 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186108707 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1e85f0f9-5093-509f-b6d5-89d20ac3fe2c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186108708 #edb/ref 1080 "images/ea/ea43acbcaa5eaf10fef44753863bafed13f64bc684f06fbd60268deee23800ea.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186108708 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186108708 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3f62843f-3df7-5523-adf2-a4d30f0843da" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110531 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7937" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110531 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the equation that generates the graph shown below.\n\n![](images/10/10f082165ef5b901e0ec43139fac54317395e1b349b31dd491dc36980981a622.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110531 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "04070131-1543-5516-a7f1-509ea3f01234" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110531 #edb/ref 1074 "To obtain the given graph, we perform the following transformations:\n\n- Take the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}$.\n- Translate the graph to the left by $1$ unit to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x+1}$.\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](images/35/3561b98dcf8113dcb644b1f3c738821f74d9f453e268fb2d47f6379d41f31951.png)\n\nTherefore, the answer is\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{x+1}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110532 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7938" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110532 #edb/ref 1071 "The graph below is a translation of $y=\\sqrt{x}$. Find the equation that generated the graph.\n\n![](images/d7/d7705be833455f266e892f78ec29f0dee88a7e3e803a00f85dfdfd15ff5f6f92.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110532 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0e964fdb-fa9e-516a-badf-2217a7937bc8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110532 #edb/ref 1074 "To obtain the given graph, we can perform the following transformations:\n\n- Take the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}$.\n- Translate the graph to the left by $2$ units to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x+2}$.\n- Translate the result down by $1$ unit to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x+2}-1$.\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](images/9a/9af181a909b6ed88cee9ab8d331a09378ed75cc85a33d0f156a5b89ac91796cf.png)\n\nTherefore, the answer is\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{x+2}-1\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110533 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7939" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110533 #edb/ref 1071 "Sketch the graph of the function $f(x) =\\sqrt{2-x}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110533 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4ffc1494-2efd-581c-a58e-d1e9a8a2dfc4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110533 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's re-write the expression as follows:\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{2-x}=\\sqrt{-(x-2)}\n$$\n\nTo obtain the graph of\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{-(x-2)}\n$$\n\nwe can perform the following transformations:\n\n- Take the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}$.\n- Reflect the graph in the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{-x}$.\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](images/08/0848b7ecf37824cfb1eabe5b9b100cd3daf545887535e691eea62686bc99d973.png)\n\n- Translate the result to the right by $2$ units to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{-(x-2)}$.\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](images/22/227210ee73219614d94bff78ddf7e0a8539dabfa2bc3b8f4778fa9292359c5f6.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110534 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7940" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110534 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the equation that generated the graph below.\n\n![](images/16/16cbb1865575a8f1d968a065a3b9a09eb6fa3b998a24029d75713825cd5b7a2a.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110534 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bc4d0d1e-4cf6-5e3a-99b8-3613593fd0d3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110534 #edb/ref 1074 "To obtain the given graph, we can perform the following transformations:\n\n- Take the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}$.\n- Reflect the graph in the $x$-axis to get the graph of $y=-\\sqrt{x}$.\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](images/78/78b19415feaf4e648e0d49a7aa3a130db5a57cf23b4aeafbdc34e5a968a3bf0e.png)\n\n- Translate the result to the left by $1$ unit to get the graph of $y=-\\sqrt{x+1}$.\n- Translate the result up by $2$ units to get the graph of $y=-\\sqrt{x+1}+2$.\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](images/4f/4ffbc7f9dd9ec50830a671f4ce688f51f6a7a11663f0c93af567ee8cc9a4a4f4.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is\n\n$$\ny = -\\sqrt{x+1}+2\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110708 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048419 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110708 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110708 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050753 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110708 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111011 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110708 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111013 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110708 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying a Square Root Function Containing One Translation" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110708 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186110531 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110708 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "a70b1e82-4650-5de9-ad47-7578481b802a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110709 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111014 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110709 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111164 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110709 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying a Square Root Function Containing Two Translations" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110709 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186110532 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110709 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "d3425852-1b32-552e-baaf-bf53644e53b8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110710 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048753 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110710 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111160 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110710 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111163 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110710 #edb/ref 1039 "Graphing a Reflected Square Root Function Containing One Translation" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110710 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186110533 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110710 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "adbab69f-d3db-5162-9c21-0402b95e0c74" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110711 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111161 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110711 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111162 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110711 #edb/ref 1039 "Graphing a Reflected Square Root Function Containing Two Translations" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110711 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186110534 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110711 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "396377cb-7e23-5c95-9f9f-a33c210bc670" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110880 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186111660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110880 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186111661 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110880 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186111662 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110880 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186111663 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110880 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186111664 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110880 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186111665 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110880 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186111666 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110880 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110880 #edb/ref 1045 "Graph Transformations of Square Root Functions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110880 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186111660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110880 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049799 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110880 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "a679a0bc-f291-575b-bac5-97356c792140" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111013 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186107781 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111013 #edb/ref 1069 "q-24153" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111013 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is the graph of $y = \\sqrt{x} - 2$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111013 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f7d38e85-9320-5cc8-bab7-c5891248f38b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111163 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186108703 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111163 #edb/ref 1069 "q-38649" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111163 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is the graph of $y = \\sqrt{-x - 1}$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111163 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4ac10221-24ce-5dfe-9994-3541ffaea81d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111660 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111661 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111660 #edb/ref 1061 464534 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111660 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2d1bbdf9-422b-5f69-8f59-21d910778f63" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111660 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186111894 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111661 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111662 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111661 #edb/ref 1061 464535 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111661 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "91171f12-b0b8-5ca8-afcf-bde7eb9fb6fe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111661 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186111895 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111662 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111663 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111662 #edb/ref 1061 464536 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111662 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "66c173b6-94ff-5b36-988c-72a5f4e6623b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111662 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110708 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111663 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111664 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111663 #edb/ref 1061 464539 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111663 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fd64edda-d116-5987-a423-30af039a0c48" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111663 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110709 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111664 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111665 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111664 #edb/ref 1061 464542 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111664 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "aa82b019-f24d-5baa-8ff4-93fdb90e7024" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111664 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186111896 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111665 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111666 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111665 #edb/ref 1061 464543 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111665 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7124301f-084e-5b5d-b8c2-4b15e1bdd17e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111665 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110710 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111666 #edb/ref 1061 464546 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111666 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "dd82d42a-f2ba-5fd4-9caa-4add435c4441" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111666 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110711 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111894 #edb/ref 1064 "The graph of the square root function\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{x}\n$$\n\nis shown below.\n\n![](images/a4/a4d6f457f29cc6a292f23029967dc6fbb0c0f3905a04f34a430fddc8b211b0c3.png)\n\nIn this lesson, we will learn how to apply graph transformations to the square root function. Let's start by considering translations." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111894 #edb/ref 1065 4775 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111894 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "ff943ba5-7959-599a-8f13-e5bdb1bda83a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111894 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111895 #edb/ref 1064 "We can move the graph of\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{x}\n$$\n\nup or down by adding or subtracting a number. For example, to obtain the graph of\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{x}-3\n$$\n\nwe perform the following transformations:\n\n- Take the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}$.\n- Translate the graph **down** by $3$ units to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}-3$.\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](images/1b/1b5eadb281202323377386e6b750a304ece8f39232d0c37dc5d4885004a6b588.png)\n\nSimilarly, we can also move the graph of\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{x}\n$$\n\nto the left or to the right by adding or subtracting a number to the variable $x$ under the square root. For instance, to obtain the graph of\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{x-3}\n$$\n\nwe perform the following transformations:\n\n- Take the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}$.\n- Translate the graph to the **right** by $3$ units to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x-3}$.\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](images/6d/6d51b569648468c78445daa6b8dc658fe6e2e8cb24ca8308b60a1f40b07c7e29.png)\n\nRemember:\n\n- Shifting a function up/down/left/right does *not* change the shape of a graph.\n- If $a$ is a positive number, then a transformation of the type $y=f(x\\pm a)$ is *counter-intuitive*: $f(x+a)$ moves the graph to the *left* by $a$ units, while $f(x-a)$ moves the graph to the *right* by $a$ units." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111895 #edb/ref 1065 4776 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111895 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "7bdd8c52-b035-531e-b5ba-085731e44771" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111895 #edb/ref 1067 "Vertical and Horizontal Translations" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111896 #edb/ref 1064 "We can reflect the graph of the square root function\n\n$$\ny = \\sqrt x\n$$\n\nin both the $x$ and $y$-axis.\n\nMultiplying the $\\sqrt x$ by $-1$ reflects the curve in the $x$-axis. The graph of\n\n$$\ny=-\\sqrt x\n$$\n\nis shown below.\n\n![](images/ee/eef724b522e133a2a537d1b6e1406bdbf17fe285ea43c278888ab4a4bc9fa58c.png)\n\nMultiplying the variable $x$ by $-1$ reflects the curve in the $y$-axis. The graph of\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{-x}\n$$\n\nis shown below.\n\n![](images/78/782eade24c5ab9e1af679f0a310fac2d3e20805d40ee97c695ea214ac71cf2f0.png)\n\nNote that\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{-x}\n$$\n\nis only defined for the negative numbers and zero.\n\nNow, suppose we want to sketch the graph of\n\n$$\ny= -\\sqrt{x-2}+3\n$$\n\nTo obtain the graph of\n\n$$\ny=-\\sqrt{x-2}\n$$\n\nwe can perform the following transformations:\n\n- Take the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}$.\n- Reflect the graph in the $x$-axis to get the graph of $y=-\\sqrt{x}$.\n\n![](images/b9/b95995b8ee5595d774f02d2c03c1170cc443b8f06f6ccbc634eeeb2aebe86357.png)\n\n- Translate the result to the right by $2$ units to get the graph of $y=-\\sqrt{x-2}$.\n- Translate the result up by $3$ units to get the graph of $y=-\\sqrt{x-2}+3$.\n\n![](images/26/263ea3a28314da17ba084bcb512976deb73483dfaa3ad149845c35634ae1d4a4.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111896 #edb/ref 1065 4777 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111896 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "55172b36-dabd-52b3-8195-cbe97b913cc0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111896 #edb/ref 1067 "Reflections" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
